# CVE-2025-47273 — setuptools: Path Traversal Vulnerability in
# setuptools PackageIndex
#
# Flagged in the apt-managed setuptools copy at
# /usr/lib/python3/dist-packages/setuptools (Debian's supervisor
# package depends on setuptools' pkg_resources module at runtime —
# see supervisor/options.py's `import pkg_resources`). This is a
# separate, older copy from the clean pip-managed setuptools used for
# everything else in this image.
#
# Risk accepted, not fixed, for a documented reason: an earlier
# attempt to delete this copy broke the container outright —
# supervisord failed to start with
# "ModuleNotFoundError: No module named 'packaging'" because
# supervisor's own startup code imports pkg_resources at runtime, not
# just at install time.
#
# The vulnerable code path itself (setuptools.PackageIndex, used for
# resolving and downloading packages from a package index over the
# network) is never invoked anywhere in this container. Nothing here
# runs `pip install`, `easy_install`, or any other setuptools
# operation at runtime — pkg_resources is imported by supervisor
# purely for its own internal metadata/plugin bookkeeping, not for
# fetching packages. There is no reachable path from this container's
# actual behavior to the vulnerable function.
#

# Revisit if: Debian ships a patched python3-setuptools release, or
# if supervisor's own dependency on pkg_resources changes in a future
# Debian package version.
CVE-2025-47273
